# Canonical author identity.
#
# Two names, one person, one email. `Rasheed Bustamam` is the GitHub profile
# display name, which GitHub stamps as the author on every squash-merge it
# creates (committer: GitHub <noreply@github.com>). `rasheed` was this machine's
# local git config, so it appears on commits pushed directly rather than merged.
#
# Without this file `git shortlog -sn` reports two contributors for a solo repo,
# and any tool that groups by author NAME splits the history. Mapping them here
# fixes that in git itself — log, shortlog, blame and `--author` all honour a
# .mailmap — with no history rewrite.
Rasheed Bustamam <rasheed.bustamam@gmail.com> rasheed <rasheed.bustamam@gmail.com>
